# Environment variables are the only sanctioned credential channel in this alpha, and a
# multi-manifest laboratory keeps one file per environment. Ignore all of them; keep the example.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# A lockfile is normally committed. This one is not portable yet: OpenSDL is unpublished, so the
# only way to install this laboratory is `uv sync --find-links` against a wheelhouse in the
# framework checkout, and uv records that local directory in uv.lock as the registry for every
# OpenSDL distribution. A clone on another machine cannot resolve it and is told nothing useful.
# Once the packages resolve from a real index, delete the `uv.lock` line below, re-lock, and commit
# the result. DEVELOPMENT.md has the full sequence.
uv.lock
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/
